# Lumen: the pooled storage daemon, installed everywhere and running
# nowhere until a pool exists.
#
# Same shape as the cluster stack's preset and for the same reason. The unit
# needs /etc/lumen/fsd.conf — a brick to serve, this node's id, and the
# peer's address — and none of that is knowable at package time. A pool is
# created by a workflow, which writes that file and starts the unit; a node
# that never joins one never runs it.
#
# Disabled rather than absent, so the unit is on disk and inspectable, and so
# an operator who enables it by hand keeps it enabled across upgrades.
disable lumen-fsd.service
